# Files listed here are never sent to the Docker build at all — Docker
# can't accidentally COPY them into the image even if a wildcard like
# "COPY . ." would otherwise include them.

# Never installed locally then shipped — we run "npm ci" INSIDE the image,
# so a node_modules built on your Windows/WSL machine (or with different
# native bindings) would be wrong Linux binaries anyway.
node_modules

# CRITICAL: your .env holds real secrets (Mongo Atlas password, JWT
# signing keys). If this got copied into the image, it would be baked into
# an image layer permanently — anyone who later pulls or inspects that
# image (e.g. if you ever push it to Docker Hub) could extract it, even
# after you "delete" the file, because old layers stay in the image
# history. Secrets get injected at container START-UP instead, via
# docker-compose's env_file — never baked in at BUILD time.
.env
.env.*

npm-debug.log*
*.log
.git
.gitignore
README.md
